SystemRequirements: PDF export of the Shiny app's recap page is rendered via
    Quarto + Typst (requires the Quarto CLI; see
    https://quarto.org/docs/get-started/) and requires a Chrome/Chromium
    binary reachable by chromote (via webshot2) to rasterize the Leaflet map
    for the static PDF. Both must be present wherever the Shiny app is
    hosted; if either is unavailable, PDF export fails gracefully with a
    Shiny notification rather than crashing the app (see
    render_recap_pdf(), R/recap_pdf.R). The recap.qmd template forces
    Chrome's --no-sandbox/--disable-dev-shm-usage/--disable-gpu launch
    flags unconditionally (see its setup chunk), since chromote's own
    is_inside_docker()/is_missing_linux_user() auto-detection did not
    reliably add them on Posit Connect Cloud's container and Chrome
    crashed (SIGABRT) on launch without them.
